---
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Kraig Spear is an iOS engineer building thoughtful apps, from personal weather tools to interactive storytelling." />
    <title>Kraig Spear — iOS Engineer</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#main" aria-label="Kraig Spear, home">Kraig Spear<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#work">Work</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="mailto:kraigspear@gmail.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Independent thinking. Native experiences.</p>
        <h1 id="intro-title">iOS Engineer.<br /><span>Made for real life.</span></h1>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <p>I’m Kraig. I build thoughtful apps for Apple platforms—turning complex ideas into experiences that feel simple.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="#work">Explore selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="work" class="work wrap" aria-labelledby="work-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="work-title">Selected work</h2><span>01 — 02</span></div>
        <article class="project klimate" aria-labelledby="klimate-title">
          <div class="project-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">01 / Personal project <span class="status">In development</span></p>
            <h3 id="klimate-title">Klimate</h3>
            <p class="project-deck">Weather, with a reason<br />to get outside.</p>
            <p>A weather app built around what you want to do. Describe an Activity in your own words; Apple’s Foundation Models help turn it into weather criteria that Swift code can evaluate against the forecast.</p>
            <p>From creating an Activity to exploring weather radar, I’m building the experience from the app’s interface through the engineering underneath.</p>
            <ul class="tags" aria-label="Klimate technologies"><li>SwiftUI</li><li>Foundation Models</li><li>Weather</li></ul>
          </div>
          <figure class="klimate-visual">
            <div class="screens">
              <img class="weather-screen" src="/images/klimate-weather.webp" width="720" height="1565" alt="Klimate weather screen showing current conditions and hourly and daily forecasts for Caledonia." fetchpriority="high" />
              <img class="activity-screen" src="/images/klimate-activities.webp" width="720" height="1565" alt="Klimate Activities screen with an enabled Morning Run activity and an add button." loading="lazy" />
            </div>
            <figcaption>A look inside the app · Development preview</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </article>
        <article class="project bible" aria-labelledby="bible-title">
          <figure class="bible-visual">
            <img src="/images/beginners-bible.jpg" width="1920" height="1440" alt="The Beginner’s Bible illustrated story selection displayed on an iPad held by a reader." loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Interactive storytelling for iPad</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="project-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / HarperCollins · 2012–2015</p>
            <h3 id="bible-title">The Beginner’s Bible</h3>
            <p class="project-deck">Little hands.<br />A world of stories.</p>
            <p>An interactive storybook with games, coloring, puzzles, and more than 400 pages of content. A shipped project from my years building mobile experiences at HarperCollins.</p>
            <p>I developed the iOS app and created StoryBook Builder, a visual authoring tool that helped the team turn illustrations and narration into interactive pages.</p>
            <ul class="tags" aria-label="The Beginner’s Bible technologies"><li>Objective-C</li><li>UIKit</li><li>Authoring tools</li></ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section id="about" class="about wrap" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Behind the apps</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="about-title">A builder, from the first idea<br />to the smallest detail.</h2>
          <p>My experience spans native iOS apps, interactive media, and the tools that make them possible. I enjoy working through the hard parts: shaping an idea, finding the right architecture, and making the finished experience feel natural.</p>
          <p>I bring the perspective of a lead engineer and the curiosity of someone who still loves writing the code.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:kraigspear@gmail.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer wrap"><p>Kraig Spear <span>· iOS Engineer</span></p><a href="https://github.com/kraigspear">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></footer>
  </body>
</html>
